# VDX Design — Cline rules

This file is a thin entry point for Cline. Two canonical documents in this
repo carry the actual instructions; read them when working on vdx-design
tasks:

1. `skills/vdx-design/SKILL.md` — the full Samsung-themed frontend skill:
   trigger conditions, theme loading, boilerplate, token usage rules, A/B
   decision flow with `vdx-decide`, and the reference docs index.

2. `skills/vdx-design/workflows/scaffold-and-bundle.md` — the scaffold-
   and-bundle workflow: how to create a new site under `<target>/src/`,
   what files to write, and how to ship a single self-contained
   `<target>/view/index.html` via `node lib/bundle.js <target>`.

## Quick triggers

- "Build a samsung-kr page" / "Use the `<theme-id>` theme" → follow
  `skills/vdx-design/SKILL.md`.
- "Scaffold a vdx site at `<dir>`" → follow the Scaffold steps in
  `scaffold-and-bundle.md`.
- "Bundle `<dir>`" / "다 만들었어, 하나로 묶어" → follow the Bundle steps
  in `scaffold-and-bundle.md` (just runs `node lib/bundle.js <target>`).

## Hard rules

- Never hardcode hex/px values in generated CSS — always `var(--vdx-…)`.
- The single-file deliverable for end users is `<target>/view/index.html`
  (CSS + JS inlined). Never tell a user to ship a multi-file site.
- Don't add npm dependencies. The project uses Node built-ins only.
- Never push directly to `main` on this repo. Land changes on a feature
  branch and open a PR.
